                <pb facs="0303" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg169"/>

                <head>No. 126.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 29,
                        1888</date>. (Received October 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 871.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    relative to the complaint of the Champerico Railway Company of San Francisco,
                    Cal., against the action of the Guatemalan Government in granting a concession
                    to Messrs. J. L. Bueron &amp; Co. to construct a parallel railway from the port
                    of Ocos to Quezaltenango, in alleged violation of a contract with the
                    former,</p>
                <p>I have the honor to transcribe the following copy and translation of a telegram,
                    dated yesterday, from the minister for foreign affairs of Guatemala, to the
                    effect that Messrs. J. L. Bueron &amp; Co. have given up their concession.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Hoy ha sido presentado al ministerio de fomento el eserito del Señor Bueron
                        en que retira su concesion.</p>
                    <p>The document of Señor Bueron, by which he surrenders his concession, has been
                        presented to-day to the minister for public works.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry C. Hall.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
